book nested_arrays_matrix
read everything from nil.std.collections

counter begin record
    field total as override integer
end record

main returns override integer begin paragraph
    value inner as array of override integer is [1, 2]
    value rows as array of array of override integer is [inner, inner, []]
    value alias is rows
    value retained is rows at 0
    set (rows at 0) at 1 to 7
    say inner at 1
    say (rows at 1) at 1
    set rows at 0 to [11, 13, 17]
    say (alias at 0) at 2
    say retained at 1
    append 19 to retained
    say the length of (rows at 1)
    append 23 to (rows at 2)
    say (rows at 2) at 0
    evaluate alias.reserve with 32
    append retained to rows
    say the length of alias
    say (rows.capacity with nothing) is at least 32

    value cube as array of array of array of override integer is [rows, [[29], []]]
    set ((cube at 0) at 1) at 0 to 31
    say inner at 0
    append 37 to ((cube at 1) at 1)
    say ((cube at 1) at 1) at 0

    value filled is new-with-value of array of override integer with size being 3, `value` being inner
    set (filled at 0) at 0 to 41
    say (filled at 2) at 0
    evaluate array-set of array of override integer with arr being filled, idx being 1, `value` being [43, 47]
    value selected is get of array of override integer with arr being filled, idx being 1
    append 53 to selected
    say (filled at 1) at 2
    say length of array of override integer with arr being filled
    say try-copy-range of array of override integer with source being filled, source-offset being 0, destination being filled, destination-offset being 1, count being 2
    set (filled at 0) at 0 to 59
    say (filled at 1) at 0
    say (filled at 2) at 0

    value object is build counter with total being 61
    value records as array of array of counter is [[object], []]
    append object to (records at 1)
    set ((records at 0) at 0).total to 67
    say object.total
    say ((records at 1) at 0).total
    give 0
end paragraph
